# Naming conventions

## Components and providers — `Ct` prefix

Applies to all files under `**/components/**` and `**/providers/**`.

- Shell / shared app UI: `modules/app/components/`, `modules/app/providers/`
- Feature UI: `modules/{feature}/components/`, `modules/{feature}/providers/`

| Item | Rule | Example |
|------|------|---------|
| File name | Start with `Ct` | `CtHeader.tsx`, `CtQueryProvider.tsx` |
| Component name | Match file | `export function CtHeader()` |
| Export | **Named export only** — no `export default` | `export function CtHeader()` |

```tsx
// modules/app/components/CtHeader.tsx
export function CtHeader() { … }

// modules/app/providers/CtQueryProvider.tsx
export function CtQueryProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>{children}</QueryClientProvider>
}
```

## Layouts — `Ct` prefix, default export

Applies to layout components under `**/layouts/**` (e.g. `CtPanelLayout.tsx`). Route files in the same folder (e.g. `_panel.tsx`) stay thin and lazy-load the layout.

| Item | Rule | Example |
|------|------|---------|
| File name | Start with `Ct` | `CtPanelLayout.tsx` |
| Component name | Match file | `export default function CtPanelLayout()` |
| Export | **Default export only** | `export default function CtPanelLayout()` |

```tsx
// modules/app/layouts/CtPanelLayout.tsx
export default function CtPanelLayout({ children }: { children?: React.ReactNode }) {
  return ( … )
}

// modules/app/layouts/_panel.tsx
export const Route = createFileRoute('/_panel')({
  component: lazy(() => import('@/modules/app/layouts/CtPanelLayout')),
})
```

## Pages — `Page` suffix

Applies to all files under `**/pages/**` (including `pages/errors/` for HTTP/error screens).

| Item | Rule | Example |
|------|------|---------|
| File name | End with `Page` | `HomePage.tsx`, `LoginPage.tsx` |
| Component name | Match file (default export name) | `export default function HomePage()` |
| Export | **Default export only** — no named page export | `export default function HomePage()` |

```tsx
// modules/app/pages/HomePage.tsx
export default function HomePage() {
  return ( … )
}
```

Route files stay thin:

```tsx
import HomePage from '@/modules/app/pages/HomePage'
```

Do **not** use names without `Ct` (components/providers) or `Page` (pages) in those folders.

Do **not** use `export default` in `components/` or `providers/` — use named exports only.

Do **not** use named exports for layout components in `layouts/` — use default export only.
